# NativMix Quality and Release Rules

## Code quality
- Lint with `ruff check lib/` (`--select I --fix` when needed).
- Type-check with `mypy lib/`.
- Prefer Python 3.10+ typing style (`X | None`).
- Never use `except Exception: pass`; log at least `logger.debug`.

## Filesystem and runtime
- Keep XDG compliance: only `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR` and `~/.config/nativmix/`.
- Do not use `/tmp/` paths.

## Packaging and releases
- Only the user runs hardware tests and installation (`makepkg`).
- Never bump versions without explicit user instruction.
- On approved version bump, update all 8 locations together:
  `pyproject.toml`, `metadata.py`, `spec`, `_service`, both `README`s, and changelog entry in `spec`.
- Escape OBS/RPM macros in comments using `%%`.
- Use `fdupes` as required by packaging flow.
